==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From {{term|seco|secō|cut, cut off|lang=la}}.

====Noun====
{{la-noun|sector|sectoris|sectōris|m|third}}

# One who [[cut]]s or [[cut off|cuts off]], [[cutter]].
# A [[purchaser]] or [[bidder]] at a sale of [[confiscated]] goods.

=====Inflection=====
{{la-decl-3rd|sector|sector|sector|sectōr}}

===Etymology 2===
Frequentative from {{term|sequor||follow|lang=la}}.

====Verb====
{{la-verb|sector|sector|sectari|sectārī|sectatus|sectātus sum}}

# I [[follow]] continually, [[attend]], [[accompany]].
# I follow after, [[pursue]], [[chase]].

